  "result": "Perfect! Foreign currency support is complete. All 310 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **RATES object** in src/money.js with exchange rates (units per euro):\n   - `EUR: 1` (no conversion)\n   - `USD: 1.085` (1 EUR = 1.085 USD)\n   - `GBP: 0.8425` (1 EUR = 0.8425 GBP)\n\n2. **convert(cents, currency)** function that:\n   - Takes amount in euro cents and target currency\n   - Converts using: `cents * RATES[currency]`\n   - Returns `ok(amountInTargetCurrencyCents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n   - Rounds to nearest cent using Math.round\n   - Example: `convert(100, 'USD')` \u2192 100 EUR cents \u00d7 1.085 = 108.5 USD cents \u2192 109 USD cents\n\n3. **formatMoney(cents, currency)** function that:\n   - Formats amount in specified currency with proper symbol\n   - `$` for USD\n   - `\u00a3` for GBP  \n   - `\u20ac` for EUR\n   - Same format as formatEuros: comma thousands separators, 2 decimals\n   - Handles negative amounts with minus sign before currency\n   - Example: `formatMoney(123456, 'USD')` \u2192 `$1,234.56`\n\n4. **UNKNOWN_CURRENCY error** added to src/errors.js for invalid currency codes\n\n5. **15 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - RATES object structure\n   - Currency conversions (EUR\u2194USD, EUR\u2194GBP, EUR\u2194EUR)\n   - Zero amounts, large amounts, negative amounts\n   - Error handling for unknown currencies\n   - Formatting in all three currencies\n   - Currency symbols and formatting consistency\n   - Integration of convert + formatMoney workflow\n\nEnables payments and invoicing in multiple currencies while maintaining all calculations in euro cents internally.",
